From 4dc1b730e03c69b4a48ef613980cf82b19039898 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:26:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 282/398] Unified: dragging stays smooth with many parts; the
 faces it touches show on top
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The faces of the other parts are read between the moves (nearest first),
straight edges without their vertices, the stacked arrays are kept while
the parts near the moving one stay the same, and the status bar is
updated between the moves (it took 10 ms): 200 parts, 3.6 ms per move
(median), 8.5 ms (95 %), in the GUI.

The outline of a face the part snaps to is drawn over everything (the
part covers the face it touches). The push/pull arrow of the pressed face
is hidden while the part moves. Views that were closed are recognised by
their widget (calling a closed view's viewer crashed). The line-up panel
opens at the top left of the 3D view, clear of the parts.

Std_Alignment is called 選んだ面に視点を向ける (it was 整列, which is
what the line-up tool is searched by).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
